 "about_text": "Peter Fetterman Gallery is a Santa Monica photography gallery founded by Peter Fetterman, a London-born collector and former filmmaker who opened his first gallery in 1988 and became one of the original tenants of Bergamot Station when it opened in 1994. The gallery holds one of the largest inventories of classic twentieth-century photography in the United States, with particular depth in humanist photography. Its holdings include work by figures such as Henri Cartier-Bresson, Sebastião Salgado, Steve McCurry, Ansel Adams, Paul Caponigro, Willy Ronis, Michael Kenna, André Kertész, Manuel Alvarez Bravo, Lillian Bassman, Pentti Sammallahti, Sarah Moon and Jeffrey Conley. The gallery presents this work in an intimate, salon-style setting intended to promote appreciation of the photographic medium.",
 "source_kind": "official",
